description:
The CameraManager.processFrame() method has a placeholder comment but doesn't actually call HandPoseDetector.

Update CameraManager.swift to:
1. Hold reference to HandPoseDetector
2. In processFrame(), call detector.processFrame(pixelBuffer)
3. Wire up callback to forward HandPose to AppDelegate

Currently at line 106: 
// The actual processing will be:
// HandPoseDetector.shared.processFrame(pixelBuffer) { [weak self] handPose in
//     self?.onFrameProcessed?(handPose)
// }

Replace this with actual implementation.
